abstract: >-
  A Hungarian-language AI-powered interactive learning platform and e-book
  covering the complete journey from conversational AI to autonomous research
  agents for scientists. 19 chapters (~100,000 words) organized in 6 parts:
  AI foundations, coding assistants, domain-specific AI (RAG, digital twins),
  agentic AI systems, institutional adoption, and domain applications
  (precision agriculture, hydroinformatics, geoinformatics). Features include
  a full book reader with markdown and LaTeX rendering; RAG-powered chat;
  209 pre-generated quiz questions (4 types: MCQ, T/F, fill-blank, essay);
  interactive concept map (99 concepts); 50+ prompt templates; and domain
  examples from the author's existing textbooks. Developed to support the
  AI transition at the University of Debrecen, aligned with Hungary's
  National AI Strategy 2025-2030.
